---
import { siteConfig } from "@/config/site"
import GithubStars from "@/components/developers/github-stars"
import HeadingAnchor from "@/components/heading-anchor"
import DevDocsLayout from "@/astro/layouts/DevDocsLayout.astro"

export const prerender = true

const repo = siteConfig.links.repo
---

<DevDocsLayout
  title="NTUMods on GitHub"
  description="Explore the NTUMods source code on GitHub, contribute to the project or give it a star."
  path="/developers/github"
  eyebrow="Community"
  heading="GitHub"
  intro="NTUMods is open source. Explore the code, suggest an improvement or help make it better.">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 id="repository">
      Explore the repository<HeadingAnchor
        id="repository"
        label="Explore the repository"
      />
    </h2>
    <p>
      The <a href={repo}>NTUMods repository on GitHub</a> contains the site, course
      data and documentation. If you find NTUMods useful, you can give the repository
      a star.
    </p>

    <GithubStars client:load repoUrl={repo} />

    <h2 id="ways-to-help">
      Ways to help<HeadingAnchor id="ways-to-help" label="Ways to help" />
    </h2>
    <p>
      You do not need to be an experienced programmer or an NTU student to
      contribute. You can report a bug, suggest an idea, fix a typo, improve
      documentation or write an article. You can also help with accessibility,
      performance or how the site works on a phone.
    </p>

    <h2 id="report-an-issue">
      Report a problem or suggest an idea<HeadingAnchor
        id="report-an-issue"
        label="Report a problem or suggest an idea"
      />
    </h2>
    <p>
      An issue is a way to start a conversation about a problem or improvement.
      You will need a free GitHub account. Visit the <a
        href={`${repo}/issues/new/choose`}>new issue page</a
      >, choose the option that fits and describe what you found or would like
      to see. For a bug, include the steps to reproduce it, what you expected
      and what happened instead. Screenshots can help too.
    </p>
    <p>
      If course data looks wrong, include the module code and semester in your
      issue. The maintainer refreshes this data, so please do not edit the data
      files yourself. For a security problem, use <a
        href={`${repo}/security/advisories/new`}>private reporting on GitHub</a
      > instead of a public issue.
    </p>

    <h2 id="first-contribution">
      Make your first contribution<HeadingAnchor
        id="first-contribution"
        label="Make your first contribution"
      />
    </h2>
    <p>
      A contribution can be a small change, such as fixing a typo. If you have
      an idea beyond a small fix, open an issue first so you can discuss the
      approach. It is fine to ask questions if you are unsure where to start.
    </p>
    <p>
      New to GitHub? Follow the <a href="/developers/github/first-contribution"
        >first contribution walkthrough</a
      > to fix a typo in your browser.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Fork the repository.</strong> On the <a href={repo}
          >repository page</a
        >, select Fork to create your own copy on GitHub.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Set up the project.</strong> Follow the <a
          href={`${repo}#getting-started`}>getting started instructions</a
        > to download your copy and run NTUMods on your computer. You will need Node.js
        and pnpm, but no Cloudflare account or secrets.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Create a branch and make your change.</strong> A branch keeps your
        work separate from the main version. Keep your change focused, and run the
        checks in the <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}
          >contribution guide</a
        > before submitting it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Open a pull request.</strong> Push your branch to GitHub, then open
        a pull request to propose your change for review. Describe what you changed
        and why. For a visual change, include a screenshot.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>contribution guide</a>
      has the full setup and checklist. If you get stuck, ask in an issue or your
      pull request. Questions are welcome.
    </p>
  </div>
</DevDocsLayout>
